```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as User
    participant LB as LB
    participant API as API
    participant PG as Postgres
    participant S3 as Object Storage
    participant RD as Redis / BullMQ
    participant W as Worker
    participant MOD as Modal

    U->>LB: POST /api/documents (multipart, Idempotency-Key)
    LB->>API: route (least-connections)

    API->>API: verify JWT
    API->>PG: atomic quota decrement (UPDATE ... WHERE balance > 0)
    alt balance = 0
        API-->>U: 403 quota_exceeded (stop)
    else balance > 0
        API->>S3: stream upload to users/{userKey}/uploads/{uuid}
        API->>RD: enqueue job
        API-->>U: 202 {jobId}
    end

    loop every 2s
        U->>API: GET /api/jobs/:id
        API->>PG: status / stage / output
        API-->>U: 202 / 200 (done / needs_review)
    end

    W->>RD: pull job
    W->>W: validating (ext/magic/script/macro/arch bomb)
    W->>S3: read upload
    W->>W: extracting (native or OCR per page)
    W->>W: structuring (2-level heading tree)
    W->>W: chunking (1 chunk / subheading)
    W->>W: assets (image sanitize, tables sanitize)
    W->>MOD: tables + images + compression (sanitized text/image only)
    W->>W: verifying (fact preservation)
    alt facts missing after 2 retries
        W->>W: condensed_status = fallback_to_original
    end
    W->>W: subject fill (if blank)
    W->>W: assemble + schema validate + completeness
    alt all checks pass
        W->>W: status = done
    else any failure
        W->>W: status = needs_review
    end
    W->>S3: write documents/{docId}.json
    W->>PG: status + output count (consumes 1 quota unit either way)

    Note over W, U: Both done and needs_review consume 1 quota unit.<br/>Rejected / failed consume 0.
```

**Parent:** L2 › Worker Process. **Notes:** idempotency key checks Redis first (step 2); quota failure stops before storage (step 3); upload streams straight to S3 (never API local disk); worker never blocks request thread.
